{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261124T154824Z-24a7cbfa", "ts": "2026-11-24T15:51:47Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "fix/credential-placeholders", "build": "391e202c37c3"}, "body": {"base_commit": "391e202c37c3f25ab208a1fd34bd31b73bb72c17", "base_tree": "240ec26ca8c7be496cbb4e1d25ced9acb634d4e3", "head_tree": "ab9ad5367082b98fb792ce6152465d45dd9dda8e", "head_commit": "8e0b0d5be1200eeec0f37e34b4a13f200dccad9b", "dispatch_commit": "8e0b0d5be1200eeec0f37e34b4a13f200dccad9b", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py", "tests/test_pr_gate.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py", "tests/test_pr_gate.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Template-shape placeholder exemptions accept open content, so a real url password shaped like a template passes the PR's credential check", "recommendation": "Scope: class. The cause is that three of the template shapes in `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` (plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py) bound the wrapper and not what is inside it, so a random string inside the wrapper is exempt. The plan's Constraint says 'A random-looking string must still be reported, so every exemption is a full match against a short, closed list', and these shapes are not closed. `\\$\\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\\}?` fullmatches `$Kx9fPq2mZ`. `\\{\\{?\\s*[A-Za-z_][\\w.]*\\s*\\}?\\}` fullmatches `{Kx9fPq2mZ}`. `<[^<>\\s]+>` fullmatches `<Xk9#mQ2vL>`. So `postgres://app:$Kx9fPq2mZ@prod/app` (a generated password that happens to start with `$`, which is literal in Python, YAML and .env files) is now reported by neither `check-pr-hygiene` nor the new exit-9 guard, and those are the only credential backstop a PR meets. Fix it through the one owner (`_is_placeholder_password`) by making the inside of each wrapper look like a placeholder too: for example the environment-variable convention `[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*` for bare `$VAR` (braced `${\u2026}` can stay as an identifier), and identifier-only content for `<\u2026>`. Re-run the 2026-11-24 corpus survey to count what the tighter shapes stop exempting. Add negative cases to `test_a_real_looking_url_password_is_still_a_credential` for a random string inside each wrapper. Today that test covers only bare random strings and a word with a suffix.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "tests/test_pr_gate.py"], "scope": "class", "closure": "A shape in `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` whose inner character class admits an arbitrary random-looking string, so the full match is closed in its wrapper but open in its content.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` \u2014 `$VAR`/`${VAR}` shape"}, {"id": "m2", "site": "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` \u2014 `{name}`/`{{ name }}` shape"}, {"id": "m3", "site": "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` \u2014 `<password>` shape"}], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "The placeholder exemption set ships a security backstop's weakening as an unconfirmed inference, and is wider than the inference states", "recommendation": "The build plan's only *Inferred:* item is the exemption set itself: '*Inferred:* the placeholder set comes from a survey ...', and it accepts on the owner's behalf that 'a real secret that happens to equal its username or a placeholder word is exempted'. The owner's recorded words ('Yes to all of your recommendations') approve placeholder exemptions in general. They do not cover these specific families or their residual risk, and planning.md says 'An inference is a decision made on the owner's behalf: never record one as their ruling.' The code in `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` also goes further than the inference describes. `\\$\\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\\}?`, `\\{\\{?\\s*[A-Za-z_][\\w.]*\\s*\\}?\\}` and `<[^<>\\s]+>` are open shapes, not entries in a closed list, so a random-looking secret is exempt whenever it is `$`-prefixed or wrapped in braces or angle brackets (`app:$Xk9mQ2vLr7@`, `app:<Xk9#mQ2vL>@`). That contradicts the plan's own constraint: 'A random-looking string must still be reported, so every exemption is a full match against a short, closed list.' The consequence: a branch carrying a real credential written in one of those forms reaches the PR without a refusal, on a tradeoff the owner never saw stated. To fix it, either get the owner to confirm the exemption set with its residual cases named (three characters or fewer, the same as the user, a placeholder word, and anything wrapped in template syntax) and record the answer in the plan's Goals, or narrow the template shapes so a random body inside the wrapper is still reported. Scope: instance. One owner, `_is_placeholder_password` / `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES`.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "scope": "instance", "closure": "The exemption predicate in backlog/transport.py that decides which url-embedded passwords credential_shape stops reporting.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py:_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES / _is_placeholder_password"}], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "record-lint governed-by-gap: .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md:18", "recommendation": "architecture carries 8 `## Direction` norm(s) but this plan disposes of 3 \u2014 each norm needs a recorded disposition, and \"inapplicable, because \u2014\" is one", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md"], "source": "record-lint", "fid": "R-3"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 3, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The plan's 'chunk/final/verify-resolutions modes dispatch' test covers only `final`", "recommendation": "Chunk 02's Tests line lists `chunk`, `final` and `verify-resolutions` as modes that dispatch on a credential-bearing branch, but `test_inner_modes_do_not_run_the_check` exercises only `final`. The guard is gated on `mode_token == \"cumulative\"`, so the risk is low. Parametrizing the test over the three modes would make it match the plan's list. No edit is required.", "files": ["tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The unreadable-span note is tested only through a monkeypatched `branch_credential_shapes`", "recommendation": "`test_an_unreadable_span_dispatches_with_a_note` replaces the producer, so nothing tests the real `unchecked` sources. Those are `_hygiene_span`'s 'could not resolve a base branch' and 'no merge-base' errors, `_credential_shape`'s unreadable-diff Result, and the broad-except branch. A fixture repo with no resolvable base would test the real producer end to end, without synthesizing its signal.", "files": ["tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "waivers.md lists fewer template forms than the code exempts", "recommendation": "The `credential-shape` row's template list (`${VAR}`, `{name}`, `<password>`) leaves out the bare `$VAR`, `{{ name }}` and `%(name)s` forms that `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` exempts. The change record lists `%(name)s`. The list reads as examples, and a reader who adds an unneeded waiver for one of the missing forms loses nothing, so this is prose only.", "files": ["plugin/docs/waivers.md"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The shape table's `is a credential` field no longer answers alone; a name test outside the table overrides it for one shape", "recommendation": "Instance. `_SECRET_SHAPES`' legend reads `(class, pattern, line form, is a credential)`, and the cloud placeholder's whole-shape exemption is expressed there. The url shape's partial exemption is instead `if name == _URL_PASSWORD and not _has_real_url_password(line)` inside `credential_shape`'s loop, so the table no longer says what the check reports, and a second partial exemption would add a second name test. If this is touched again, replace the boolean with an optional per-shape predicate (`None` = always a credential, `lambda m: False` for the cloud placeholder, the placeholder test for the url shape), so one table states every exemption. Localized and named by a constant, so no edit is owed now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "The template and mask exemptions are wider than 'visibly a placeholder' (for correctness to rate)", "recommendation": "waivers.md and the plan's constraint say every exemption is a full match on something visibly a placeholder. Two `_PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD_SHAPES` admit more than that: `\\$\\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\\}?` fully matches any identifier-shaped password with a leading `$`, so `$ecretP4ss` is exempt, and `<[^<>\\s]+>` matches any non-space text in angle brackets. Whether that is a real backstop gap is Goal 1's to rate, not this role's. If it is tightened, `\\$\\{[^}]+\\}|\\$[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*` keeps the `$PG_PASS` / `${PG_PASS}` forms the tests pin.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "plugin/docs/waivers.md"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The credential remedy now has a second home in the CLI, beside /prawduct:pr Step 3", "recommendation": "Instance. `cmd_critic_begin`'s exit-9 message restates pr/SKILL.md:122 almost word for word (treat it as leaked, rotate it, rewrite the branch; otherwise the waiver on the line or the one above), and it hard-codes `prawduct/credential-shape` where `pr_gate.CREDENTIAL_WAIVER` and `RESULT_MEANINGS[\"credential-shape\"]` already own the waiver form. The waiver syntax is documented as fixed, so nothing drifts today. If the remedy changes, build the waiver token from `pr_gate.CREDENTIAL_WAIVER` rather than adding a third copy.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "begin_review's docstring lists its return shapes and leaves out the new credential refusal", "recommendation": "Instance, docstring wording. The `Returns` paragraphs list each status and kind with its CLI exit (ok, error/scope-widened, no-review-needed, budget-exhausted, precondition-failed, chunks-ambiguous). `{\"status\": CREDENTIAL_REFUSED, \"findings\"}` (exit 9) is missing, and it carries no `reason`, so a new caller that handles 'anything not ok' the way the CLI's generic branch does (`result['reason']`) would raise a KeyError. The only caller today handles it first, so nothing breaks. No edit is owed unless the docstring is touched.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Placement of the placeholder rule deepens the credential concern inside the GitHub transport module", "recommendation": "Recorded decision (the plan's 'every fact has one home' disposition), so this is not a finding. `backlog/transport.py` describes itself as 'the sole egress to GitHub'. It now also holds a placeholder classifier that only the PR gate's check uses (`scrub_secrets` ignores it), and its consumers are pr_gate, critic_consolidate (through pr_gate), git_hygiene and evidence_sync. If the denylist grows again, a `lib/credentials.py` that transport re-exports would give it a home that matches its consumers.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "Records Pass: covered files_oracle (api-contract.md, build-plan-credential-placeholders.md, changes/credential-placeholders.md). Nothing clears a bar", "recommendation": "Covered all three oracle records. api-contract.md: the `--force` list (exit 3, 4, 7, 9) matches begin_review, since exit 8 chunks-ambiguous really does ignore force. The exit-9 Error Model entry matches the code: refused before scope or tree capture, stdout gives file, line and shape, one guard-refusal fact with a line count and no text, and an unreadable span dispatches with a note. The change record and plan claims match the code, except the change record's 'a real-looking secret ... is still reported'. That sentence is false only for the template-wrapped edge covered by the finding on transport.py, and it is fixed by that finding's remedy, so no separate record finding. record_lint's governed-by-gap is consolidation's and is not restated.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "The survey figures behind the exemption set cannot be re-derived", "recommendation": "The plan's tradeoff cites '202 url-embedded password matches ... exempts 181 ... keeps 21' from a survey of every governed repo on this machine. No command or script is recorded. Authoring rule 'A spike that discards its code leaves its numbers unfalsifiable \u2014 commit the derivation as a runnable script and cite the COMMAND, never the digits.' The corpus is other repos, so the digits cannot be committed, but the command could be. Nothing reads the figures, so no edit is owed for this round.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "A consumer repo name enters this repo for the first time", "recommendation": "`hearsay` appears nowhere at the base and is introduced by tests/test_pr_gate.py (the `hearsay:password@localhost/hearsay` fixture) and the build plan ('In hearsay the waiver comment landed...'). `metallm` already appears across the repo, so naming consumers may be accepted practice. Core rule 'Before the first write to a shared surface (push, issue, PR, comment, artifact) after reading private sources, check its visibility and grep the payload for their names' applies before this is pushed to a possibly public origin. A neutral fixture name would cost nothing.", "files": ["tests/test_pr_gate.py", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md"], "oid": "O-11"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "Goal 6 clean: the new guard can be observed both when it fires and when it cannot look", "recommendation": "A refusal records one `critic-dispatch-credential-shape` guard-refusal fact through the shared sink, which stats.py groups by guard. A failure to record is printed to stderr by `_record_guard_refusal`. A span that cannot be read, or a raised check, becomes `unchecked` and then a dispatch note naming the cause, and is never counted as clean. The PR gate still fails closed on the same condition. No growing collections. No edit wanted.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py"], "oid": "O-12"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "credential-placeholders", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02"], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {"01": {"paths": ["plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "paths_more": 0, "commits": ["a23e5e3d7ec4"]}, "02": {"paths": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py"], "paths_more": 1, "commits": ["8e0b0d5be120"]}}, "base_reviewed": "391e202c37c3f25ab208a1fd34bd31b73bb72c17", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md", "plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", "findings": [{"check": "governed-by-gap", "path": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", "line": 18, "detail": "architecture carries 8 `## Direction` norm(s) but this plan disposes of 3 \u2014 each norm needs a recorded disposition, and \"inapplicable, because \u2014\" is one"}], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 1, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0, "late-requirement-record": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "no-boundary-review", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-24T15:48:29Z"}}

